{"id":"79d1f1cfd5e6220d32e60e3e39367bbb289251b5","axis":"silent","repo":"vimeo/psalm","sha":"79d1f1cfd5e6220d32e60e3e39367bbb289251b5","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"config.xsd","lines":["@@ -256,6 +256,7 @@","             <xs:element name=\"CheckType\" type=\"IssueHandlerType\" minOccurs=\"0\" />","             <xs:element name=\"CircularReference\" type=\"IssueHandlerType\" minOccurs=\"0\" />","             <xs:element name=\"ClassMustBeFinal\" type=\"IssueHandlerType\" minOccurs=\"0\" />","+            <xs:element name=\"CliOnlyCall\" type=\"IssueHandlerType\" minOccurs=\"0\" />","             <xs:element name=\"ComplexFunction\" type=\"IssueHandlerType\" minOccurs=\"0\" />","             <xs:element name=\"ComplexMethod\" type=\"IssueHandlerType\" minOccurs=\"0\" />","             <xs:element name=\"ConfigIssue\" type=\"IssueHandlerType\" minOccurs=\"0\" />"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/running_psalm/error_levels.md","lines":["@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@ These issues have very low false-positive rates and indicate definite problems."," ","  - [AbstractMethodCall](issues/AbstractMethodCall.md)","  - [CheckType](issues/CheckType.md)","+ - [CliOnlyCall](issues/CliOnlyCall.md)","  - [ComplexFunction](issues/ComplexFunction.md)","  - [ComplexMethod](issues/ComplexMethod.md)","  - [ConfigIssue](issues/ConfigIssue.md)"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/running_psalm/issues.md","lines":["@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@","  - [CheckType](issues/CheckType.md)","  - [CircularReference](issues/CircularReference.md)","  - [ClassMustBeFinal](issues/ClassMustBeFinal.md)","+ - [CliOnlyCall](issues/CliOnlyCall.md)","  - [ComplexFunction](issues/ComplexFunction.md)","  - [ComplexMethod](issues/ComplexMethod.md)","  - [ConfigIssue](issues/ConfigIssue.md)"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/running_psalm/issues/CliOnlyCall.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@","+# CliOnlyCall","+","+Emitted when code that may run outside the command line calls a function, method or class marked `@psalm-cli-only`.","+","+```php","+<?php","+","+/**","+ * @psalm-cli-only","+ */","+final class ImportCommand","+{","+    public function run(): void","+    {","+        echo 'Importing ' . (string) ($_SERVER['argv'][1] ?? '') . \"\\n\";","+    }","+}","+","+function handleRequest(): void","+{","+    (new ImportCommand())->run();","+}","+```","+","+## Why this is bad","+","+What `@psalm-cli-only` code prints isn't reported as `TaintedHtml`, because it goes to a terminal. Called from a web request, it goes to the HTTP response instead.","+","+## How to fix","+","+Mark the caller `@psalm-cli-only` too, or check the SAPI first. The check covers the code it guards, like any other assertion:","+","+```php","+<?php","+","+/**","+ * @psalm-cli-only","+ */","+function import(): void {}","+","+/**","+ * @psalm-cli-only","+ */","+function run(): void","+{","+    import(); // no issue","+}","+","+if (PHP_SAPI === 'cli') {","+    import(); // no issue","+}","+","+import(); // CliOnlyCall","+","+if (php_sapi_name() !== 'cli') {","+    exit(1);","+}","+","+import(); // no issue","+array_map(fn(string $file) => import(), ['a.csv']); // no issue","+```"],"additions":61,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/running_psalm/upgrading_to_psalm_7.md","lines":["@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@ The rest of this page covers what some projects will notice. The complete list o"," - **Callmap return types distinguish documentation from signatures.** Implementations of internal interfaces with only a documentary return type no longer need a native declaration. Native and PHP 8.1+ tentative signatures still require compatible returns, with `#[ReturnTypeWillChange]` applying only to tentative signatures. Tools reading the dictionary files must support their [compact format](../contributing/editing_callmaps.md#full-callmap-format)."," - **Taint analysis runs by default**, in the same run as type checking, and is faster than a separate `--taint-analysis` run (see the [release notes](https://github.com/vimeo/psalm/releases/tag/7.0.0)). To run type checking only, set `runTaintAnalysis=\"false\"`."," - **New security findings.** If taint analysis reports more than you want to deal with at once, you have these tools ([docs](https://psalm.dev/docs/security_analysis/avoiding_false_positives/)):","-    - `@psalm-cli-only` on a function, method or class: what its code prints is not reported as `TaintedHtml`;","+    - `@psalm-cli-only` on a function, method or class, or a `PHP_SAPI === 'cli'` check: what that code prints is not reported as `TaintedHtml`;","     - `<taintAnalysis><ignoreFiles>` in `psalm.xml`: taint paths through the listed files and directories (tests, for example) are not reported;","     - `@psalm-taint-specialize`: each call of a function or each instance of a class is tracked separately;","     - `runTaintAnalysis=\"false\"`: turn it off."],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/security_analysis/avoiding_false_positives.md","lines":["@@ -102,9 +102,10 @@ echo processVar($_GET['text'], true); // considered secure"," ## Output of command-line code"," "," What a script run from the command line prints goes to a terminal or a log, not to an HTML page. `@psalm-cli-only` on","-a function, a method or a class says that it only runs from the command line: what its code (and the closures in it)","-prints with `echo`, `print`, `printf()`, `vprintf()`, `var_dump()`, `debug_zval_dump()`, and `print_r()` and","-`var_export()` not returning it, isn't reported as `TaintedHtml`.","+a function, a method or a class says that it only runs from the command line, and so does a `PHP_SAPI` or","+`php_sapi_name()` check for the code it guards: what that code (and the closures in it) prints with `echo`, `print`,","+`printf()`, `vprintf()`, `var_dump()`, `debug_zval_dump()`, and `print_r()` and `var_export()` not returning it, isn't","+reported as `TaintedHtml`."," "," ```php"," <?php","@@ -120,11 +121,18 @@ final class ImportCommand","         echo 'Importing ' . $file . \"\\n\"; // not reported","     }"," }","+","+if (PHP_SAPI !== 'cli') {","+    exit(1);","+}","+","+(new ImportCommand())->run();","+echo $_SERVER['argv'][1] ?? ''; // not reported"," ```"," ","-Printing a secret is still reported, and the values stay tainted for every other sink. The annotation only covers the","-code it is on: a method of another class, or a function, called from there is checked as usual, so annotate it too if","-it only runs from the command line.","+Code marked `@psalm-cli-only` can only be called from such code, or [CliOnlyCall](../running_psalm/issues/CliOnlyCall.md)","+is reported. Printing a secret is still reported, and the values stay tainted for every other sink. A function called","+from command-line code is checked as usual, so mark it too if it only runs from the command line."," "," ## Sanitizing HTML user input"," "],"additions":14,"deletions":6,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Psalm/Context.php","lines":["@@ -58,6 +58,12 @@ final class Context","      */","     public const PHP_VERSION_ID_VAR_ID = 'PHP_VERSION_ID';"," ","+    /**","+     * The pseudo-variable through which comparisons of the PHP_SAPI constant and of php_sapi_name() narrow them, so","+     * a branch knows the SAPI it runs in (e.g. `if (PHP_SAPI === 'cli')`); it can't clash with a variable name.","+     */","+    public const PHP_SAPI_VAR_ID = 'PHP_SAPI';","+","     /**","      * @var array<string, Union>","      */"],"additions":6,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Psalm/Internal/Analyzer/ClosureAnalyzer.php","lines":["@@ -362,6 +362,13 @@ public static function analyzeExpression(","             }","         }"," ","+        // a closure runs on the PHP version and in the SAPI of the code creating it","+        foreach ([Context::PHP_VERSION_ID_VAR_ID, Context::PHP_SAPI_VAR_ID] as $var_id) {","+            if (isset($context->vars_in_scope[$var_id])) {","+                $use_context->var